From: xcentaurix
Subject: [PATCH] Skia: resolve glGetFloatv through the epoxy core functions, not eglGetProcAddress (GrGLContext::Make failed on the Broadcom V3D driver)

Symptom (VU+ Ultimo 4K, Broadcom V3D-435, "OpenGL ES 2.0"): GrDirectContexts::MakeGL returns null although the GL interface is created and glGetError is 0, so
Skia has no GPU context (see 0021: the web process used to crash, now the compositor is invalidated and nothing is painted).

Cause: MakeGL -> GrGLGpu::Make -> GrGLContext::Make -> GrGLInterface::validate(). The GL version ("OpenGL ES 2.0") and the GLSL version ("OpenGL ES GLSL ES
1.00") both parse, and validate() lists glGetFloatv among the functions that must exist whatever the GL version. The epoxy interface
(GrGLMakeEpoxyEGLInterface.cpp) hands Skia the core functions listed in GR_GL_CORE_FUNCTIONS_EACH from epoxy itself and asks eglGetProcAddress() for every
other name. glGetFloatv is the one required function missing from that list. The EGL spec only guarantees eglGetProcAddress() for extension functions
(EGL_KHR_get_all_proc_addresses is what makes it return core ones): Mesa answers, Broadcom's libEGL returns NULL, fGetFloatv stays null and validate() fails.

Fix: add glGetFloatv to the list, like its siblings glGetError / glGetIntegerv. No change on drivers whose eglGetProcAddress already answered.

Same family, GL ES only: validate() also requires glInsertEventMarkerEXT / glPushGroupMarkerEXT / glPopGroupMarkerEXT whenever GL_EXT_debug_marker is
advertised. The Broadcom V3D driver (VU+ Ultimo 4K) advertises it and may not export them. Skia's GL backend never calls them, so the ES requirement is dropped.

---
--- a/Source/ThirdParty/skia/src/gpu/ganesh/gl/GrGLCoreFunctions.h	2026-10-31 10:24:47.700602300 +0200
+++ b/Source/ThirdParty/skia/src/gpu/ganesh/gl/GrGLCoreFunctions.h	2026-10-31 10:25:37.496203700 +0200
@@ -66,6 +66,7 @@
     M(glGenerateMipmap) \
     M(glGetBufferParameteriv) \
     M(glGetError) \
+    M(glGetFloatv) \
     M(glGetFramebufferAttachmentParameteriv) \
     M(glGetIntegerv) \
     M(glGetProgramInfoLog) \
--- a/Source/ThirdParty/skia/src/gpu/ganesh/gl/GrGLInterfaceAutogen.cpp	2026-10-31 10:40:49.561743700 +0200
+++ b/Source/ThirdParty/skia/src/gpu/ganesh/gl/GrGLInterfaceAutogen.cpp	2026-10-31 10:40:49.563727700 +0200
@@ -584,10 +584,8 @@
         }
     }
 
-    if ((GR_IS_GR_GL(fStandard) && (
-          fExtensions.has("GL_EXT_debug_marker"))) ||
-       (GR_IS_GR_GL_ES(fStandard) && (
-          fExtensions.has("GL_EXT_debug_marker")))) {
+    // (GL ES: not required. Skia's GL backend never calls the markers, and some ES drivers advertise GL_EXT_debug_marker without exporting the functions.)
+    if (GR_IS_GR_GL(fStandard) && fExtensions.has("GL_EXT_debug_marker")) {
         if (!fFunctions.fInsertEventMarker ||
             !fFunctions.fPopGroupMarker ||
             !fFunctions.fPushGroupMarker) {
